respectful response checked by an adult for protocol; revise if any appropriation appears. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: original example using respectful response on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Sample error: Imitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect.. Correction: Strong answer: All four moves;. Why it helps the audience is stated.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Imitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect. Respect means listening and crediting. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating respectful response on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with respectful response, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Accept original work about respectful response with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material. / Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for respectful response. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"This matches the taught method for respectful response. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["All four moves; no invented sacred content","Imitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect","A claim that names no evidence from the lesson material","A method that skips the key step taught in this lesson"],"question":"Write a respectful paragraph with credit, description, limit sentence and one non-appropriative connection. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"This is the misconception to avoid for respectful response; the other choices align with the lesson method. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Careful use of credit and explain why it matters with clear evidence","Imitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect","A respectful written response describes what you read/heard, credits the creator and source, states the limit of your","All four moves; no invented sacred content"],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when working with respectful response?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and a named credit and explain why it matters, not by copying the model. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Imitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect","Name credit and explain why it matters only, without linking it to respectful response","Apply respectful response to new material and name the credit and explain why it matters used","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence"],"question":"Which response best applies respectful response with new evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"The skill is shown by quoting or pointing to wording that carries respectful response. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Point to exact words in the sentence that show respectful response and say what they do","Ignore the sentence and invent a more exciting event","Say the writing is good without naming any words","Imitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect"],"question":"Read: \"In the dusty shed, Lila oiled the bike chain before the race.\" Which choice best uses respectful response from this lesson?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the language skill with textual evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Imitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect","Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged","Name credit and explain why it matters without linking it to any words in the text","All four moves; no invented sacred content"],"question":"Which statement correctly applies the lesson idea about respectful response?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Start from a specific textual clue, then explain its effect. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Copy a model sentence from another story unchanged","Lengthen the answer with adjectives while keeping the same idea","Locate precise textual evidence, then explain how language choices shape meaning or effect","Guess from the title alone with no textual clue"],"question":"In a new text, what should you do first to analyse credit and explain why it matters?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Repair means fixing meaning or evidence, not padding. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Add adjectives without fixing the wrong idea","Make the answer longer while keeping the same mistake","Delete the evidence that disagreed with your first guess","Change the inaccurate idea or missing evidence, not only the length"],"question":"Which revision actually improves meaning for respectful response?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Accurate transfer needs fresh material with an explained language choice. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Change fonts and claim the work is new","Imitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect","Use a fresh sentence or text and explain one precise choice about respectful response","Retype the worked model as the final answer"],"question":"Which response shows accurate use of respectful response on fresh material?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept original work about respectful response with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material.","question":"Produce a fresh example demonstrating respectful response on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.","sample_answer":"Sample: original example using respectful response on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for respectful response. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea.","question":"Name one likely error with respectful response, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.","sample_answer":"Sample error: Imitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect.. Correction: Strong answer: All four moves;. Why it helps the audience is stated.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent task and reflection, with explanations where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s4-eng-y7-w29-l2","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA alignment; verify content points before acceptance.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S4","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise respectful response.","Read the mission before you start writing or speaking.","Keep the audience and purpose in mind as you work."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your reason with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the evidence."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the wording that carries the meaning.","Then explain the choice without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore the example.","Prefer evidence over wording that merely sounds clever."],"submit":["Check that your response and reason are both present.","Proofread names, sequence and punctuation.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact word or action before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and underline one useful detail.","Say what that detail helps a reader understand.","A vague compliment is weaker than quoted evidence."],"teach2":["Compare a weak attempt with a stronger revision.","Change meaning or accuracy, not only length.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose a fresh topic that still uses the same skill.","Explain one decision in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include an original response and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new content."]},"subject":"English","success_criteria":["I can use respectful response with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify credit and explain why it matters.","I can practise limit of knowledge independently on a new prompt.","I can notice personal connection without appropriation needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"A respectful written response describes what you read/heard, credits the creator and source, states the limit of your knowledge about restricted meanings and may connect personally without claiming cultural ownership or rewriting sacred material.","options":["A guess with no explanation","A claim unrelated to the text","A respectful written response describes what you read/heard, credits the creator and source, states the limit of your","An answer copied without understanding"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about respectful response with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nModel: ''I read [title] by [creator] (approved anthology). I noticed… I do not know restricted meanings beyond what the text shares. Connection: the theme of listening carefully matters in my family too—without claiming the story as mine.''\n\nTRY FIRST\nWrite a respectful paragraph with credit, description, limit sentence and one non-appropriative connection.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: All four moves; no invented sacred content.","explain":"A respectful written response describes what you read/heard, credits the creator and source, states the limit of your knowledge about restricted meanings and may connect personally without claiming cultural ownership or rewriting sacred material.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Imitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect. Respect means listening and crediting. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Writing a respectful response.","caption":"See the process.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Teach</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">what/why/how</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Model</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">worked example</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which detail matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the exact words or actions that carry the meaning before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: Model: ''I read [title] by [creator] (approved anthology). I noticed… I do not know restricted meanings beyond what the t Then write your own attempt.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which detail matters most.\nJuno: Name the exact words or actions that carry the meaning before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this model: Model: ''I read [title] by [creator] (approved anthology). I noticed… I do not know restricted meanings beyond what the t Then write your own attempt."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader.","options":["A claim unrelated to the text","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no explanation","Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about respectful response with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nModel: ''I read [title] by [creator] (approved anthology). I noticed… I do not know restricted meanings beyond what the text shares. Connection: the theme of listening carefully matters in my family too—without claiming the story as mine.'' Think about how this word or relationship creates meaning.\n\nTRY FIRST\nUnderline or quote one precise detail in the model and explain its effect.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful evidence is a specific choice in the example, followed by an explanation of the effect on meaning.","explain":"Make your choice visible: select the exact detail in the model that demonstrates the skill, and describe what it does for a reader.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Saying a choice is good without naming the actual detail does not show understanding. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Explain the evidence","visual":[{"alt":"Learning loop.","caption":"Evidence over guess.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Practise</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">guided then independent</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Reflect</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">criteria check</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison.","options":["A guess with no explanation","A claim unrelated to the text","Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison","An answer copied without understanding"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about respectful response with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nImitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect. Respect means listening and crediting. Here is a more productive model: Model: ''I read [title] by [creator] (approved anthology). I noticed… I do not know restricted meanings beyond what the text shares. Connection: the theme of listening carefully matters in my family too—without claiming the story as mine.''\n\nTRY FIRST\nDescribe why the warned-against approach would weaken your work, then write a corrected version.\n\nFEEDBACK\nStrong answer: All four moves; no invented sacred content.","explain":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific error, then show how a revision fixes that error.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"A superficial change in length or appearance does not repair meaning. Imitating dialect or sacred symbols for effect. Respect means listening and crediting. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Test a misconception"},{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Use the method on a new topic, not a reworded copy of the example.","options":["An answer copied without understanding","Use the method on a new topic, not a reworded copy of the example","A guess with no explanation","A claim unrelated to the text"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about respectful response with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nA respectful written response describes what you read/heard, credits the creator and source, states the limit of your knowledge about restricted meanings and may connect personally without claiming cultural ownership or rewriting sacred material. Now choose different people, facts or text to show you can transfer the idea.\n\nTRY FIRST\nMake one fresh example demonstrating the skill and explain your main choice.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe new example should meet the same purpose as the model, but contain original material.","explain":"Use the method on a new topic, not a reworded copy of the example. Review the result for accuracy and reader clarity.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner make decisions based on specific language evidence, rather than guess or copy someone else. Keep the meaning accurate and explain the choice.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the original example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new content. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Transfer to an independent example"}],"title":"Year 7, Week 29, Lesson 2: Writing a respectful response","unit_number":8,"unit_title":"Australian voices and identity","week":29,"week_in_unit":1,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\nModel: ''I read [title] by [creator] (approved anthology). I noticed… I do not know r